(7539333, 1206442, 19959, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by 3DsArcher:</b></div><hr/><i> I hope you got shelter before the storm arrived. That looks like it was about to bucket down. Nicely captured </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I did not. I neglected to check the direction that this weather was moving and it caught me. It was almost instantly soaked to the skin. I was on my way to the office and spent the day wet. :(</td>', 'Originally posted by 3DsArcher: I hope you got shelter before the storm arrived. That looks like it was about to bucket down. Nicely captured  I did not. I neglected to check the direction that this weather was moving and it caught me. It was almost instantly soaked to the skin. I was on my way to the office and spent the day wet. :(', '2017-10-16 04:51:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(7539334, 1206466, 100393, '<td valign="top">Why do people think this was flipped. It might be crap, but it isn''t flipped.</td>', 'Why do people think this was flipped. It might be crap, but it isn''t flipped.', '2017-10-16 05:04:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(7539335, 1206010, 28742, '<td valign="top">Way to go, Deb! Beautiful!</td>', 'Way to go, Deb! Beautiful!', '2017-10-16 05:51:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(7539336, 1206484, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge well<br/> <br/>Congratulations Ronnie, a well deserved ribbon. Another lovely image, the strong focal point of the egret in the most appropriate hotspot is what makes this impressive image really stand out. I also particularly like the distorted reflection and the mist adds a real atmosphere and calmness against the birds hunting tension. Well done Ronnie.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge well Congratulations Ronnie, a well deserved ribbon. Another lovely image, the strong focal point of the egret in the most appropriate hotspot is what makes this impressive image really stand out. I also particularly like the distorted reflection and the mist adds a real atmosphere and calmness against the birds hunting tension. Well done Ronnie.', '2017-10-16 06:48:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(7539337, 1206476, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>I like your low viewpoint Janine that puts an emphasis on the foreground water, I think without this it would struggle as a waterscape given the prominence of the rocky surroundings, as it is they are still rather too dominating. The motion of the water is about right plenty of motion but not so much as all detail is lost, a pleasing balance. A pleasing image, thanks Janine.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge I like your low viewpoint Janine that puts an emphasis on the foreground water, I think without this it would struggle as a waterscape given the prominence of the rocky surroundings, as it is they are still rather too dominating. The motion of the water is about right plenty of motion but not so much as all detail is lost, a pleasing balance. A pleasing image, thanks Janine.', '2017-10-16 06:53:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(7539338, 1206325, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that does not meet the challenge<br/> <br/>Although you have a pleasing composition, I feel this is more of a landscape with water than what the challenge should be about a waterscape, i.e., where the water dominates the image. What I think could have worked a lot better would have been to go in really close to the water with a wide angle lens and really make that water dominate the scene. I think the section just before the bend at the right angle and close enough you could have made that look like a giant waterfall?</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that does not meet the challenge Although you have a pleasing composition, I feel this is more of a landscape with water than what the challenge should be about a waterscape, i.e., where the water dominates the image. What I think could have worked a lot better would have been to go in really close to the water with a wide angle lens and really make that water dominate the scene. I think the section just before the bend at the right angle and close enough you could have made that look like a giant waterfall?', '2017-10-16 07:00:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(7539339, 1206170, 152725, '<td valign="top">Thank you for comment, those are water droplets as the wind was blowing towards my lens. Not really dust on my sensor. I did not have a lens cloth with me at that point. Will take note for future shooting.</td>', 'Thank you for comment, those are water droplets as the wind was blowing towards my lens. Not really dust on my sensor. I did not have a lens cloth with me at that point. Will take note for future shooting.', '2017-10-16 08:30:36.000000', NULL, 0),
